connection to the Internet using a Web browser (such as Mosaic)
that is capable of handling "forms". Forms allow users to enter
data into their browser for processing by Open Market. Most
browsers today can handle forms. Most computers today have
methods for connecting to the Internet through a local Internet
Service Provider (ISP). 

